IMPORT prelude

-- State Lands Protection Act 2022 (Singapore) -- what counts as State land (s 3), the unauthorised-activities offence and its
-- penalties and defences (ss 5-7), the vehicle owner's duty to name the driver (s 10), encroachment notices and what follows (ss 12-14),
-- forfeiture of abandoned land and the limit on compensation (ss 17-20), obstruction (s 26) and composition (s 27).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 29/5/2026", of Act 42 of 2022, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SLPA2022.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The only amendment
-- annotated in the deposit is "[Act 8 of 2026 wef 29/05/2026]" (the Sewerage, Drainage and Coastal Protection Act renaming in
-- ss 3(4)(b) and 32(1)(c)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0070 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to the provisions a person or business meets: whether land is State land, what may not be done on it, the penalties, the
-- encroachment-notice procedure, forfeiture of abandoned land, and dealings with officers. Not encoded: interim injunctions (s 9),
-- the magistrate's complaint procedure beyond its trigger (s 16), the detail of enforcement powers (ss 21-24), disposal of seized
-- things (s 25), administration (ss 28-31), corporate and partnership liability (ss 34, 35), service of documents (s 37), the
-- court's additional orders on conviction (s 8), the subterranean-structure defence (s 7(2)), and the amendments, repeal and
-- transitional provisions (ss 40-46).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Lands Protection Act 2022 -- State land`

§§ `3 -- meaning of State land`

-- s 3(1): State land means land in Singapore (a) "that is unalienated land"; (b) that vests in the Government and remains unalienated;
-- (c) surrendered to the Government and remains unalienated; or (d) "the subject of a notification in the Gazette made under ... section
-- 3 or 5 of the Land Acquisition Act 1966 unless the notification is cancelled before possession of the land is taken".
-- (5): "unalienated land" means land for which "no grant ... or lease, and no licence to occupy" has been issued under the Foreshores
-- Act, the State Lands Act or the 1886 Ordinances.
-- (2): land CEASES to be State land if (a) it is sold or lawfully contracted to be sold and the price "has been received by the
-- Government", whether or not the purchaser is registered; or (b) it is contracted to be sold by award of tender "and the deposit has
-- been received". (3): land under (2)(b) "becomes State land again if the purchaser fails to complete the purchase".
-- (4): NOT State land for this Act: national parks, nature reserves, public parks and green verges under the Parks and Trees Act; drainage
-- reserves; land in the cross-border railway area; railway premises; a public street; a street reserve vested in the Government; a
-- backlane vested in the Government.
DECLARE Parcel IS ONE OF
    `ordinary vacant land`
    `a national park, nature reserve or public park`
    `green verges managed by the National Parks Board`
    `a drainage reserve`
    `land in the cross-border railway area`
    `railway premises`
    `a public street`
    `a street reserve`
    `a backlane`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parcel is carved out by s 3(4)` IF
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `ordinary vacant land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel,
      `a grant, lease or licence to occupy has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gazetted for compulsory acquisition and not cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sold and the price received` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `tender deposit received` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tender purchaser failed to complete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is State land` IF
        (NOT `the parcel is carved out by s 3(4)` `the parcel`)
    AND (    (NOT `a grant, lease or licence to occupy has been issued`)
         OR  `gazetted for compulsory acquisition and not cancelled`)
    AND (NOT `sold and the price received`)
    AND (    (NOT `tender deposit received`)
         OR  `the tender purchaser failed to complete`)

§ `Improper use of State land`

§§ `5 -- unauthorised activities`

-- s 5(1): "A person commits an offence if the person, without lawful authority, intentionally" does any of: (a) occupy or live on State
-- land; (b) erect a structure; (c) clear, dig up or cultivate; (d) interfere with any substance (s 5(4): including remove, quarry,
-- extract, stack and heap); (e) deposit or leave waste, goods or any other thing; (f) park or leave any vehicle or vessel; (g) damage or
-- enclose; (h) cut, remove or damage vegetation; (i) take forest products; (j) abandon or release an animal; (k) cause or allow any of
-- these. s 2: "lawful authority" means "with the permission of the Authority, or as required or allowed by or under any written law".
-- (2): an arrestable offence. (3): the prosecution need NOT prove that the accused "knew or had reason to believe" the land is State land.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `living in a hut on the land`
    `putting up a fence`
    `growing vegetables`
    `taking away sand`
    `dumping renovation debris`
    `parking a lorry`
    `cutting down a tree`
    `releasing a pet rabbit`
    `letting a contractor dump there`
    `photographing the land`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is listed in s 5(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `photographing the land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(1): "it is a defence ... for the accused to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that the accused did not know, and could not
-- reasonably have been expected to know, that the land concerned was State land". The burden is the accused's.
-- (s 7(2), a defence for subterranean structures under the State Lands Act easement of support, is not encoded.)
GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity,
      `on State land` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved could not reasonably have known it was State land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty of a s 5 offence` IF
        `the activity is listed in s 5(1)` `the activity`
    AND `on State land`
    AND (NOT `with lawful authority`)
    AND `intentionally`
    AND (NOT `proved could not reasonably have known it was State land`)

§§ `6 -- penalty`

-- s 6(3): "motor vehicle" means a vehicle that (a) is propelled wholly or partly by a motor, or other non-human, non-animal means;
-- (b) "has 4 or more wheels"; and (c) is used or intended to be used on any road.
GIVEN `wheels` IS A NUMBER, `motor-propelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `used on roads` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a motor vehicle under s 6(3)` IF
    `motor-propelled` AND `wheels` AT LEAST 4 AND `used on roads`

-- s 6(3): a "repeat offender" for s 5(1)(e) is a person convicted of the current offence "committed involving the use of a motor vehicle
-- or vessel" who has, "within the period of 5 years immediately before" that conviction, been convicted of the same offence involving
-- a motor vehicle or vessel, or of an offence under s 7(1)(b) of the repealed 1883 Act involving one. (Whether an earlier conviction
-- exactly 5 years before counts is not decided here; the encoding treats "within" as at most 5 years, an inference.)
GIVEN `the current dumping involved a motor vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an earlier dumping conviction involved a motor vehicle or vessel` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years from the earlier conviction to this one` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender` IF
        `the current dumping involved a motor vehicle or vessel`
    AND `an earlier dumping conviction involved a motor vehicle or vessel`
    AND `years from the earlier conviction to this one` AT MOST 5

-- s 6(1): "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or ... both" and, for a continuing offence,
-- "a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- (2): a repeat offender dumping (s 5(1)(e)) by motor vehicle or vessel, or causing or allowing it: "$100,000 or ... 12 months".
GIVEN `a repeat motor-vehicle dumper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a s 5 offence` MEANS
    IF `a repeat motor-vehicle dumper` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

GIVEN `a repeat motor-vehicle dumper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for a s 5 offence` MEANS
    IF `a repeat motor-vehicle dumper` THEN 12 ELSE 6

GIVEN `days or part days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine for a continuing s 5 offence` MEANS
    `days or part days continued after conviction` TIMES 500

§§ `10 -- naming the driver`

-- s 10(1): where the driver or a passenger of a motor vehicle (or vessel, (4)) is suspected of a s 5(1)(e) offence, the owner "must give
-- any information that the owner may be required to give ... as to the identity and address" of the driver or passenger. (2): a person
-- who, "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply ... within 14 days after the date on which the information was required" -- fine
-- up to $10,000. (3): not excused on the ground that the information "might tend to incriminate the person".
GIVEN `gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days after the request` IS A NUMBER,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner commits the s 10 offence` IF
        (    (NOT `gave the information`)
         OR  `days after the request` GREATER THAN 14)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§ `Encroachment notices`

§§ `12 -- the notice`

-- s 12(1): an authorised officer with "reasonable cause to believe" a person is committing a s 5 offence may give an encroachment notice;
-- (2) it may direct the person to leave, demolish a structure, remove things, stop removing things, or do rectification works.
-- (3) it must state a compliance period and an objection period; (4) "The objection period ... must not be longer than the compliance
-- period". (5) a person who does not object within the objection period must comply "so far as is reasonably practicable and at the
-- person's cost" within the compliance period; (6) failing to comply "without reasonable excuse" -- fine up to $10,000.
GIVEN `objection period in days` IS A NUMBER, `compliance period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice periods are lawful` IF
    `objection period in days` AT MOST `compliance period in days`

GIVEN `objected within the objection period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `complied within the compliance period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to comply with the notice is an offence` IF
        (NOT `objected within the objection period`)
    AND (NOT `complied within the compliance period`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 15(2): an objection must "be signed by the person who makes it" and "state the basis for the person's authority" to occupy, build,
-- carry on the activity, or claim an interest in the structure. s 16(1): on receiving an objection an authorised officer MAY complain to a
-- Magistrate; (3), (4): a party claiming title may apply for a stay, which the Magistrate MUST grant "if ... satisfied that the claim is
-- genuine", pending the High Court.
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `states the basis of authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is in proper form` IF
    `in writing` AND `signed` AND `states the basis of authority`

GIVEN `claims title to the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Magistrate is satisfied the claim is genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Magistrate must stay the proceedings` IF
    `claims title to the land` AND `the Magistrate is satisfied the claim is genuine`

§§ `13, 14 -- the Authority steps in`

-- s 13(1): where the person "fails to do so within the compliance period and does not give the Authority an objection ... within the
-- objection period", the Authority may (a) carry out the work and (b) direct a deposit "within a period ... being at least 7 days after
-- the direction is given".
GIVEN `objected within the objection period` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied within the compliance period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may carry out the notice` IF
    (NOT `objected within the objection period`) AND (NOT `complied within the compliance period`)

GIVEN `days allowed to pay the deposit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposit direction allows enough time` IF
    `days allowed to pay the deposit` AT LEAST 7

-- s 13(6): an owner of removed material who is "not ... a person in default" and claims after it was sold, destroyed or disposed of
-- under (5) but "before the end of one year starting the date the removed material was moved or removed", MAY be compensated "for the
-- loss of the removed material, less reasonable costs and expenses" of storing and selling or disposing of it. The text gives no
-- floor; treating a negative balance as nothing is an inference.
GIVEN `a person in default` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since removal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may be compensated for removed material` IF
    (NOT `a person in default`) AND `days since removal` LESS THAN 365

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` x MEANS
    IF x LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE x

GIVEN `value lost` IS A NUMBER, `storage and sale costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most compensation for removed material` MEANS
    `not below zero` (`value lost` MINUS `storage and sale costs`)

-- s 14(1): expenses reasonably incurred are "recoverable from the person in default"; (4) a sum unpaid "at the end of one month starting
-- the date the certificate ... is given, or any further period that the Authority may allow ... is deemed to be arrears".
GIVEN `months since the certificate was given` IS A NUMBER, `further months allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unpaid expenses are arrears` IF
    `months since the certificate was given` GREATER THAN 1 PLUS `further months allowed`

§ `Resumption of land`

§§ `17, 18 -- forfeiture of abandoned land`

-- s 17: land "abandoned for 3 years or more" by the person to whom it was alienated, or anyone claiming through them, "shall be forfeited
-- to the State even though some person may be found in occupation". s 18(1): a Collector, with the Minister's approval, declares it
-- liable to forfeiture; (2) a resumption notice is published in the Gazette; (3) failure to publish "does not invalidate the
-- declaration"; (4) if, "at the end of 3 months after the day on which a resumption notice is published", nobody appears with a claim,
-- or the claimant "has not exercised the person's right to recover possession", the land "is deemed forfeited".
-- The 3 months run from publication, so the encoding requires publication for deemed forfeiture (an inference: s 18(3) saves the
-- declaration, not the running of the period).
GIVEN `years abandoned` IS A NUMBER,
      `declared with the Minister's approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `resumption notice published` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `a claimant has sued to recover possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is deemed forfeited` IF
        `years abandoned` AT LEAST 3
    AND `declared with the Minister's approval`
    AND `resumption notice published`
    AND `months since the notice` AT LEAST 3
    AND (NOT `a claimant has sued to recover possession`)

-- s 19: a person who "within a period of 6 years after the date of forfeiture" establishes a claim is entitled to "any sum that the
-- Minister may direct, which sum cannot exceed the appraised value of that land" as at the date the forfeiture notice was gazetted.
GIVEN `years since forfeiture` IS A NUMBER, `appraised value at gazettal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most compensation for forfeited land` MEANS
    IF `years since forfeiture` AT MOST 6 THEN `appraised value at gazettal` ELSE 0

§§ `20 -- no adverse possession`

-- s 20: "No State land shall be acquired by possession or unlawful occupation, and the provisions of the Limitation Act 1959 shall not
-- apply to any action brought by the Government for the recovery of State land."
GIVEN `years of occupation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `occupation gives title to State land` IF
    `years of occupation` LESS THAN 0 AND FALSE

GIVEN `years since the occupation began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government's claim to recover is time-barred` IF
    `years since the occupation began` LESS THAN 0 AND FALSE

§ `Dealing with officers`

§§ `26 -- obstruction`

-- s 26(1): intentionally failing to do what s 22(1) requires, or "knowingly obstructs or prevents, or attempts to obstruct or prevent",
-- an officer -- "$10,000 or ... 12 months or ... both". (3): "It is not an offence under subsection (1) for any person to refuse to
-- comply with any request ... made ... by any authorised officer or enforcement officer who fails to declare his or her office and
-- refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
-- (2): removing or tampering with an affixed encroachment notice or summons -- "$5,000 or ... 6 months or ... both".
GIVEN `refused to comply` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the officer declared the office` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the officer produced the card on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal is an offence under s 26(1)` IF
        `refused to comply`
    AND (`the officer declared the office` OR `the officer produced the card on demand`)

§§ `27 -- composition`

-- s 27(1): a specially authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by
-- collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of": (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence";
-- (b) "$5,000". Which offences are prescribed is in regulations not deposited here.
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can be` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 LESS THAN 5000 THEN `the maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE 5000
